                <zone fixed-size='1114' forceUpdate='true' h='3059' id='137' type-v2='text' w='80142' x='17571' y='11412'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'>→</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8'> This filter only applies for the shares that are calculated compared to platform data (second diagrams for orders, GMV and customers). Definitions:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='7' italic='true'>* Wallet order:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='7' italic='true'> orders that were made exclusively using wallet. It&apos;s the wallet purchase value and corresponds to the data shown in the first diagrams. </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='7' italic='true'>* Wallet customer (or user):</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='7' italic='true'> user that did a wallet payment in the calendar month/quarter, regardless of all additional payments done. The values that consider wallet customers take into consideration all transactions made during the period by those customers. </run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
